     <section anchor="interaction-with-bridges" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4">
       <name slugifiedName="name-interaction-with-bridges">Interaction with Bridges</name>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-4-1">802.1d MAC bridges which connect different media, for example
-Ethernet and FDDI, have become very widespread.  Some of them do IPv4
-packet fragmentation and/or support IPv4 Path MTU discovery [RFC
-1981], many others do not, or do so incorrectly.  Use of IPv6 in a
-bridged mixed-media environment must not depend on support from MAC
-bridges, unless those bridges are known to correctly implement IPv6
-Path MTU Discovery [RFC 1981, ICMPV6].</t>
-      <t indent="0" pn="section-4-2">For correct operation when mixed media are bridged together by
-bridges which do not support IPv6 Path MTU Discovery, the smallest
-MTU of all the media must be advertised by routers in an MTU option.
-If there are no routers present, this MTU must be manually configured
-in each node which is connected to a medium with a default MTU larger
-than the smallest MTU.</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-4-1">802.1d MAC bridges which connect different media, for example Ethernet and FDDI, have become very widespread.  Some of them do IPv4 packet fragmentation and/or support IPv4 Path MTU discovery <xref target="RFC-1981" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC 1981"/>, many others do not, or do so incorrectly.  Use of IPv6 in a bridged mixed-media environment must not depend on support from MAC bridges, unless those bridges are known to correctly implement IPv6 Path MTU Discovery <xref target="RFC-1981" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC 1981"/>, <xref target="ICMPV6" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="ICMPV6"/>.</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-4-2">For correct operation when mixed media are bridged together by bridges which do not support IPv6 Path MTU Discovery, the smallest MTU of all the media must be advertised by routers in an MTU option. If there are no routers present, this MTU must be manually configured in each node which is connected to a medium with a default MTU larger than the smallest MTU.</t>
     </section>
